# WHICH GOVERNANCE COMMIT THIS COMMIT WAS VERIFIED AGAINST.
#
# governance/ (schema, sql, sp, tests) lives in a separate PRIVATE repository
# and is no longer a submodule -- it used to appear as a gitlink entry in this
# repository's file listing, which read as though the private material were
# published here. It never was: a gitlink is a commit id, and every clone of
# that path 404s without access.
#
# But the gitlink was doing one real job besides fetching, and this file keeps
# it: it recorded WHICH governance commit a given public commit was verified
# against. Without a pin, CI would verify each commit against whatever
# governance/main happened to be at the time, and a green tick would no longer
# identify what was actually checked. That is the same class of defect as a
# test that passes for the wrong reason.
#
# Update this whenever governance changes, in the same commit that depends on
# the change -- exactly as the gitlink had to be updated.
